WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:01.470
Hey guys.

00:00:01.470 --> 00:00:05.870
So, this video will admittedly be something
completely different today.

00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:09.660
Because I wanna introduce to you guys a new
series that I’ve discovered this week and

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:12.100
also discuss its latest chapter a little.

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:15.530
The series I’m talking about is Kaiju number
8.

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:20.220
I stumbled across it when looking for a new
series to start on Mangaplus and it’s actually

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:25.580
listed as the 8th most popular series there
at the moment, even before the likes of chainsaw

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:27.970
man or Jiujutsu Kaisen.

00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:32.270
And since there are only 9 chapters so far
and the cover art looked pretty damn awesome,

00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:34.380
I figured I’d give it a go.

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:38.150
And holy shit, what a story it is.

00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:42.990
if you want to start reading before watching
this video, all 9 chapters are free to read

00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:43.990
so far.

00:00:43.990 --> 00:00:47.730
The link is in the description below, just
make sure to come back afterwards.

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:52.820
There are a number of familiar concepts in
here that we already know from other manga,

00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:57.730
but so far that really doesn’t seem to be
a bad thing at all.

00:00:57.730 --> 00:00:59.380
Just the opposite.

00:00:59.380 --> 00:01:05.290
The series, written and illustrated by Naoya
Matsumoto takes place in modern-day Tokyo.

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:10.830
The only difference is that for some still
unknown reason enormous monsters pop up to

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:14.880
harass the people at times, threatening civilisation.

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:19.990
To counter this, the country has created the
so called defence force, which’s sole purpose

00:01:19.990 --> 00:01:23.090
is to destroy these enormous creatures.

00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:28.800
Their strongest member is Mina Ashiro a tough-looking
woman that we see destroy one of these gigantuous

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:31.770
beasts with relative ease.

00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:36.860
Up top this point the story carries some aspects
of both attack on titan as well as pacific

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:37.860
rim.

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:43.391
However Kaiju no 8 addresses an issue that
most giant monster stories gloss over: What

00:01:43.391 --> 00:01:46.800
happens once these beasts have been killed?

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:50.619
This is where the main character of the story
comes into play.

00:01:50.619 --> 00:01:56.560
The 32 year old Kafka, who’s name is drawn
from the 20th century author Franz Kafka,

00:01:56.560 --> 00:02:01.060
dreamed of joining the defence force, but
has failed to pass the entrance exam multiple

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:03.770
times and has given up on his dream.

00:02:03.770 --> 00:02:06.210
Kafka was childhood friends with Mina.

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:11.150
The two made a vow to join the Defense Force
and protect Japan from the Kaiju together

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:14.090
after seeing their town destroyed.

00:02:14.090 --> 00:02:19.950
After failing to follow Mina however, he has
joined the so-called Kaiju Cleanup Corp instead.

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:24.731
His job as a Monster Sweeper is to chop up
and dispose of Kaiju killed by the Defense

00:02:24.731 --> 00:02:25.731
Force.

00:02:25.731 --> 00:02:30.640
And so for a change, we learn about the nasty
side of killing large creatures in a civilian

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:33.720
area and how to lean up the mess they leave.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:39.450
However, everything changes for Kafka, when
the ambitious 18-year-old Ichikawa is assigned

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:40.930
to work with Kafka.

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:45.700
Ichikawa also has plans to take the exam to
become a member of the Defense Force and with

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:50.910
his strong determination manages to ignite
Kafka’s will once again.

00:02:50.910 --> 00:02:55.340
After being attacked by a so-called YoJu,
smaller monsters that accompany the main Kaiju

00:02:55.340 --> 00:03:01.730
when they emerge, both Kafka and Ichikawa
stand their ground, but end up in the hospital.

00:03:01.730 --> 00:03:07.940
There Kafka is infected by a small parasite-like
monster and suddenly his body transforms into

00:03:07.940 --> 00:03:11.420
a small, but powerful monster himself.

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:15.569
When another monster appears in the city,
he defeats it with ease and is from here on

00:03:15.569 --> 00:03:19.910
out known as Kaiju number 8, wanted by the
public.

00:03:19.910 --> 00:03:25.530
This is of course a reference to Franz Kafka’s
story the Metamorphosis, where the main character

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:29.040
one day wakes up transformed into a giant
insect.

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:33.220
From here on out, Kafka learns to control
his new powers at will and with his new-found

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:38.160
strength he and Ichikawa participate in the
next entrance exam.

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:40.560
Here they meet Kikoru Shinomiya.

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:45.270
Kikoru is the daughter of the Defense Force
Commander and her Combat Power is greater

00:03:45.270 --> 00:03:46.960
than any of the other applicants.

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:51.560
Kikoru is viewed as the hope for Japan and
the future leader of the Defense Force, but

00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:55.640
suffers heavily under her fathers high expectations.

00:03:55.640 --> 00:04:00.790
During the exam, she easily disposes of the
smaller monsters that have been set as obstacles,

00:04:00.790 --> 00:04:03.940
similar to the entrance exam in my hero academia.

00:04:03.940 --> 00:04:08.780
Kikoru defeats most of them, including the
main monster in a short amount of time.

00:04:08.780 --> 00:04:15.220
However, suddenly a mysterious humanoid Kaiju,
similar to Kafka’s transformation appears,

00:04:15.220 --> 00:04:18.660
who revives the monster and gives it a power-up.

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:22.449
Quickly it defeats Kikoru and threatens to
kill her.

00:04:22.449 --> 00:04:27.320
In the last moment, Kafka decides to reveal
his power in front of her and takes out the

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:29.139
monster with ease.

00:04:29.139 --> 00:04:33.010
In the latest chapter, we see the aftermath
of the fight and learn that he mysterious

00:04:33.010 --> 00:04:37.860
monster has infiltrated the Monster Sweeper
force by taking up human appearance.

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:42.919
Now, obviously should I decide to keep going
with this series, I will make the chapter

00:04:42.919 --> 00:04:45.060
reviews much more thoroughly.

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:49.540
However, since this is the very first video
on this, and most of you probably have just

00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:54.011
heard about this story for the very first
time, I’d prefer to share with you, why

00:04:54.011 --> 00:04:57.070
I have such high hopes for this manga.

00:04:57.070 --> 00:05:01.760
Despite sharing elements with other popular
manga, I believe that up to this point all

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:06.130
of them have been presented in a quite unique
and interesting way.

00:05:06.130 --> 00:05:10.380
The fact that so little is explained about
the world and how these creatures came to

00:05:10.380 --> 00:05:14.930
be in the first place, hint at something larger
being at work here and it feels like this

00:05:14.930 --> 00:05:20.040
story might have quite a bunch of things to
be revealed and explored over time, promising

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:24.050
some great world building, no pun intended.

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:28.960
In this sense it gives me great Attack on
Titan vibes as well, but in a more than positive

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:29.970
way.

00:05:29.970 --> 00:05:36.030
The art style also is really nice, reminding
me at times of both Boku no Hero and Fire

00:05:36.030 --> 00:05:37.530
Force.

00:05:37.530 --> 00:05:42.400
Most importantly for me however, the characters
all seem to be more than promising, as in

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:48.130
the handful of chapters we have so far, there
is already a lot happening in terms of characterisation

00:05:48.130 --> 00:05:51.290
and shaping complex personalities.

00:05:51.290 --> 00:05:56.160
In addition to the excellent action, good
plotting and pacing, and quality character

00:05:56.160 --> 00:06:00.020
work, Matsumoto also delivers some wonderful
comedy.

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:04.550
The buddy team of Kafka and Ichikawa have
created some excellent chemistry between the

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:08.199
different characters in such a short time.

00:06:08.199 --> 00:06:13.350
The story also promises to have a great balance
between fun Shounen vibes and some darker

00:06:13.350 --> 00:06:16.789
and more mature elements, which I personally
am a big fan off.

00:06:16.789 --> 00:06:17.789
Matsumoto also delivers tons of gorgeous artwork.

00:06:17.789 --> 00:06:20.770
Many of the panels are flat out wonderful
to look at.

00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:26.600
All of them are meticulously drawn and the
action is kinetic and leaps off the page.

00:06:26.600 --> 00:06:30.600
Facial expressions, and emotions are also
wonderfully captured.

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:35.240
Combined with great writing and a good balance
between inner and outer dialogue, every chapter

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:38.570
so far has really captured me completely.

00:06:38.570 --> 00:06:44.600
And so, overall, Kaiju No. 8 is a brilliant
and fun read that delivers great chapter after

00:06:44.600 --> 00:06:47.800
great chapter, getting me excited for the
next one.

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:52.600
While it’s still too early to make such
predictions, I think that the story has enormous

00:06:52.600 --> 00:06:55.729
potential and I highly recommend checking
out it out.

00:06:55.729 --> 00:06:58.120
You will not be disappointed.

00:06:58.120 --> 00:07:01.320
So, once you have checked out the story yourself,
please let me know if this is something you

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:03.639
would like me to cover on a weekly basis.

00:07:03.639 --> 00:07:07.350
It really depends on your feedback and preference.

00:07:07.350 --> 00:07:11.229
So make sure to share your thoughts with me
in the comments below.

00:07:11.229 --> 00:07:12.229
Thanks guys.

00:07:12.229 --> 00:07:12.230
Peace.

